{"type": "answer", "run_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "rpm_halved", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q3", "request_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z-0003", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:19.895+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 38.525, "patience_s": 23.71, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 2922.8, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z-0003", "question": "How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "kind": "answer", "level": 1, "text": "The Transformer adds a positional encoding vector to each token embedding, where the encoding has the same dimension \\(d_{\\text{model}}\\) and is defined by sine and cosine functions of varying frequencies: for even indices \\(2i\\) it uses \\(\\sin(\\text{pos}/10000^{2i/d_{\\text{model}}})\\) and for odd indices \\(2i+1\\) it uses \\(\\cos(\\text{pos}/10000^{2i/d_{\\text{model}}})\\) so that each dimension corresponds to a sinusoid whose wavelength forms a geometric progression [S1].  \nThese sinusoidal encodings were chosen because a fixed offset \\(k\\) between positions can be expressed as a linear function of the original encodings, making it easy for the model to learn relative positions [S1].  \nThe authors also tried learned positional embeddings and found that performance was nearly the same as with sinusoids [S2].  \nHowever, they preferred the sinusoidal version because it can generalize to sequence lengths longer than those seen during training, whereas learned embeddings are limited to the lengths they were trained on [S1][S2].", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.6 §3.5", "pid": "attention:2400:0011", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b004", "attention-p06-b005", "attention-p06-b006", "attention-p06-b007", "attention-p06-b008", "attention-p06-b009"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "1706.03762v7 pp.8-9 §6.2", "pid": "attention:2400:0020", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p08-b012", "attention-p08-b013", "attention-p09-b001", "attention-p09-b002", "attention-p09-b003", "attention-p09-b004", "attention-p09-b005"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "1706.03762v7 pp.7-8 §5.4", "pid": "attention:2400:0018", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p07-b015", "attention-p08-b001", "attention-p08-b002", "attention-p08-b003", "attention-p08-b004"]}], "notice": "answered by a fallback model because the preferred one was busy; checked for citations only (no second-model check)", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 239, "completion_tokens": 56}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1321, "completion_tokens": 394}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.8, "model": null, "outcome": "full (other model)", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 30.691437600005884, "openai/gpt-oss-20b": 1.9735644000029424, "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-20b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 321.1, "model": null, "outcome": "router", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 0.9, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:understand", "start_ms": 0.9, "end_ms": 321.0, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 321.1, "end_ms": 321.3, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "sinusoidal positional encoding formula absolute position relative ordering property How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "papers": ["attention"], "k": 3, "evidence": {"best": 0.719, "union": 0.719, "top_bm25": 56.081, "query_terms": 7}}}, {"name": "decide", "start_ms": 321.3, "end_ms": 321.4, "model": null, "outcome": "draft", "detail": {"best": 0.719, "union": 0.719, "top_bm25": 56.081, "query_terms": 7}}, {"name": "draft", "start_ms": 321.4, "end_ms": 2921.6, "model": null, "outcome": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "detail": {"level": "full (other model)"}}, {"name": "wait:draft", "start_ms": 321.4, "end_ms": 1987.1, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 1.672}}, {"name": "call:draft", "start_ms": 1987.1, "end_ms": 2921.5, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "check", "start_ms": 2921.6, "end_ms": 2922.5, "model": null, "outcome": "pass", "detail": {"gate_ok": true, "failures": 0, "verifier": null}}, {"name": "verify", "start_ms": 2922.4, "end_ms": 2922.5, "model": null, "outcome": "skipped (no headroom)", "detail": {}}, {"name": "send", "start_ms": 2922.5, "end_ms": 2922.5, "model": null, "outcome": "answer", "detail": {}}], "checks": {"gate": {"ok": true, "sentences": 4, "failures": []}, "verifier": null, "draft_model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "attempts": 1, "router": {"papers": ["attention"], "query": "sinusoidal positional encoding formula absolute position relative ordering property How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "alt_query": "learned position embeddings addition input position information How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?"}, "retrieval": {"query": "sinusoidal positional encoding formula absolute position relative ordering property How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "papers": ["attention"], "k": 3, "pids": ["attention:2400:0011", "attention:2400:0020", "attention:2400:0018"]}}, "released_ms": 2922.5, "budget_wait_ms": 1665.8, "tokens_in": 1560, "tokens_out": 450, "level_name": "full (other model)", "pipeline_model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 239, "completion_tokens": 56, "tokens_estimated": false, "ms": 319.89550000434974, "waited_s": 0.0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1321, "completion_tokens": 394, "tokens_estimated": false, "ms": 933.9972999950987, "waited_s": 1.672}]}}
{"type": "answer", "run_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "rpm_halved", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q8", "request_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z-0004", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:21.736+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 40.363, "patience_s": 17.28, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 1188.7, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z-0004", "question": "What are Moshi's main components and what does each do?", "kind": "answer", "level": 1, "text": "Moshi’s architecture is built around three core components: the Helium text‑language‑model backbone, the Mimi neural audio codec, and the streaming Depth Transformer that jointly processes two audio streams and time‑aligned text tokens [S2]. Helium supplies strong reasoning and linguistic knowledge to the system by providing pre‑trained text tokens that are used as prefixes for semantic generation, thereby improving factuality and linguistic quality during dialogue [S1][S2]. Mimi encodes raw audio into discrete acoustic tokens using residual vector quantization and distills semantic information into the first token level, enabling the model to synthesize intelligible, high‑quality speech directly from its predictions without a separate TTS stage [S1][S3]. The Depth Transformer, designed for streaming inference, hierarchically generates semantic and acoustic tokens for both the user and Moshi while aligning text tokens via the Inner Monologue procedure, allowing full‑duplex, real‑time spoken dialogue without explicit speaker‑turn modeling [S1][S3].", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2410.00037v1 pp.6-7 §3.1", "pid": "moshi:2400:0009", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p06-b005", "moshi-p07-b001", "moshi-p07-b002"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.6 §2", "pid": "moshi:2400:0008", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p06-b001", "moshi-p06-b002"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.3 §1", "pid": "moshi:2400:0003", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p03-b003", "moshi-p03-b004", "moshi-p03-b005", "moshi-p03-b006", "moshi-p03-b007", "moshi-p03-b008"]}], "notice": "answered by a fallback model because the preferred one was busy; checked for citations only (no second-model check)", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 231, "completion_tokens": 82}, {"step": "draft", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1745, "completion_tokens": 294}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 1.0, "model": null, "outcome": "full (other model)", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 34.0534375999996, "openai/gpt-oss-20b": 44.29056440000568, "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 1.0, "end_ms": 401.2, "model": null, "outcome": "router", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:understand", "start_ms": 1.0, "end_ms": 1.0, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:understand", "start_ms": 1.0, "end_ms": 401.1, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 401.2, "end_ms": 401.7, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "Moshi architecture Inner Monologue Time Extended Transformer TTT Residual Vector Quantization RVQ streaming autoregressive What are Moshi's main components and what does each do?", "papers": ["moshi"], "k": 3, "evidence": {"best": 1.0, "union": 1.0, "top_bm25": 28.523, "query_terms": 5}}}, {"name": "decide", "start_ms": 401.7, "end_ms": 401.8, "model": null, "outcome": "draft", "detail": {"best": 1.0, "union": 1.0, "top_bm25": 28.523, "query_terms": 5}}, {"name": "draft", "start_ms": 401.8, "end_ms": 1187.4, "model": null, "outcome": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "detail": {"