{"type": "answer", "run_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "rpm_halved", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q13", "request_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z-0005", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:23.176+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 41.813, "patience_s": 14.33, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 3.9, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z-0005", "question": "In H-Net, what do the encoder and decoder networks do, and at what resolution do they run?", "kind": "passages", "level": 3, "text": "No written answer this time: here are the most relevant passages from the papers, quoted as they are. A written answer should be possible in about 9 s.\n[S1] 2507.07955v2 pp.19-20 §3.3: \"A natural question arises: does the importance of Mamba layers (i) stem specifically from processing fine-grained byte inputs, or (ii) because they are better for compressing information into the next stage, even at coarser input resolutions? To investigate these hypotheses, we train a 1-stage H-Net on top of BPE-tokenized inputs processed by the GPT-2 tokenizer. We then evaluate six different encoder-decoder combinations.\"\n[S2] 2507.07955v2 pp.4-5 §2.1.1: \"H-Net employs a hierarchical architecture comprising three primary components – encoder networks (E), main network (M), and decoder networks (D) – where each component is implemented with a stack of sequence mixing layers (e.g., Transformers or state space models). In its simplest form, a single-stage H-Net consists of one encoder network, one main network, and one decoder network. Crucially, the architecture’s key characteristic lies in the main network’s unique property: it can itself be instantiated as a complete H-Net, enabling recursive construction of multi-level hierarchies.\"", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2507.07955v2 pp.19-20 §3.3", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0035", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p19-b005", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b006", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b007", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b009", "dynamic_chunking-p20-b001"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2507.07955v2 pp.4-5 §2.1.1", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0007", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p04-b013", "dynamic_chunking-p04-b014", "dynamic_chunking-p04-b015", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b001", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b002", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b003", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b004", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b005", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b006", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b007", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b009"]}], "notice": "passages only, no model call: no drafter free within 8 s", "eta_s": 8.8, "model_calls": [], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.9, "model": null, "outcome": "passages", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 35.150437600008445, "openai/gpt-oss-20b": 17.27623869999661, "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": 30.46922620000987}, "lean": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 26.795437600005243, "openai/gpt-oss-20b": 8.801238699998066, "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": 21.739226200013945}}, "drafter": null}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 0.9, "end_ms": 1.4, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "In H-Net, what do the encoder and decoder networks do, and at what resolution do they run?", "papers": null, "k": 2, "evidence": {"best": 0.728, "union": 0.728, "top_bm25": 13.078, "query_terms": 7}}}, {"name": "send", "start_ms": 3.8, "end_ms": 3.8, "model": null, "outcome": "passages", "detail": {}}], "checks": {}, "released_ms": 3.8, "budget_wait_ms": 0, "tokens_in": 0, "tokens_out": 0, "level_name": "passages", "pipeline_model_calls": []}}
{"type": "answer", "run_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "rpm_halved", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q9", "request_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z-0001", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:14.602+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 33.241, "patience_s": 41.1, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 11629.4, "degraded": false, "reply": {"request_id": "rpm_halved-20261110T183141Z-0001", "question": "What makes Moshi full-duplex, and how does it handle both sides speaking at once?", "kind": "answer", "level": 0, "text": "Moreover, Inner Monologue decomposes speech on a per-frame basis, which means that each prediction step outputs a speech frame. [S1]", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.5 §2", "pid": "moshi:2400:0007", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p05-b001", "moshi-p05-b002"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.6 §2", "pid": "moshi:2400:0008", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p06-b001", "moshi-p06-b002"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.1 Abstract", "pid": "moshi:2400:0000", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p01-b005"]}], "notice": "checked for citations only (no second-model check)", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 237, "completion_tokens": 56}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1463, "completion_tokens": 51}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.6, "model": null, "outcome": "full", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 0.0, "openai/gpt-oss-20b": 0.0, "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 0.6, "end_ms": 414.1, "model": null, "outcome": "router", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:understand", "start_ms": 0.7, "end_ms": 0.7, "model":